{{!
    @template enrol_apply/manage_actions

    The decisions of the applications queue, rendered into a core sticky footer: the live count
    of the selection, then Cancel applications, Defer and Confirm (MQ-D4), the review page's order
    and styles.

    Only the actions live here. The decision's own inputs - the groups, the role, the message and
    the note - stay in the page body, because a core sticky footer is a fixed 80px bar whose
    .sticky-footer-content carries overflow hidden, so a textarea would be clipped.

    Each button is a submit named formaction with its decision as the value, so without JavaScript
    one press posts the selection, the queue's POST contract unchanged. With JavaScript
    enrol_apply/manage takes the click over and opens the decision sheet instead (MQ-D5, MQ-D6).

    Every button carries the toggle-all action vocabulary: data-action toggle, data-toggle action,
    and the group name, which core matches exactly rather than by prefix. None ships the disabled
    attribute, unlike core's own participants page: the queue is operable without JavaScript, so
    amd/src/manage.js disables them on init instead (see its docblock). That depends on the rule in
    styles.css that brings the sticky footer on screen when no script ran, because core parks one
    off screen until its own JavaScript slides it in.

    Each button carries its full label and a short one, and the stylesheet shows the short one below
    576 px, where the bar must keep one line. The full label is the button's accessible name at
    every width, and contains the short one.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * togglegroup string - name of the core/checkbox-toggleall group the table's rows belong to
    * selectedlabel string - the count of selected rows, worded "on this page" because that is
      what a selection is: refreshTableContent() replaces the whole table region on a page turn,
      a sort or a filter change, so every checkbox in it is destroyed and the count starts again
    * actions array - value, label, short and classes (the button's style) for each decision

    Example context (json):
    {
        "togglegroup": "enrol-apply-queue",
        "selectedlabel": "0 selected on this page",
        "actions": [
            {"value": "cancel", "label": "Cancel applications", "short": "Cancel", "classes": "btn-outline-danger"},
            {"value": "wait", "label": "Defer", "short": "Defer", "classes": "btn-outline-secondary"},
            {"value": "confirm", "label": "Confirm", "short": "Confirm", "classes": "btn-primary"}
        ]
    }
}}
<div class="enrol_apply-formaction d-flex align-items-center gap-2">
    <span class="enrol_apply-selectedcount small text-muted" data-region="selectedcount"
        aria-live="polite">{{selectedlabel}}</span>
    {{#actions}}
        <button type="submit" class="btn {{classes}} enrol_apply-decide" name="formaction" value="{{value}}"
            aria-label="{{label}}" data-region="decide"
            data-action="toggle" data-toggle="action" data-togglegroup="{{togglegroup}}"><span
            class="enrol_apply-decide-long" aria-hidden="true">{{label}}</span><span
            class="enrol_apply-decide-short" aria-hidden="true">{{short}}</span></button>
    {{/actions}}
</div>
